    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d750">

                <pb facs="0979" n="877" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg877"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">384.11/9: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">George</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis Ababa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-06-29T12:00:00+02:35">June 29,
                            1935—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 2:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>49. Department’s June 26, 2 p.m. American missionaries in capital who would
                    follow advice to depart are prepared to depart immediately. A certain number may
                    be expected to insist on remaining out of sense of duty. Potential danger varies
                    according to locality outside capital and I have recommended immediate
                    evacuation some stations. British Minister conferring with Emperor, and I shall
                    telegraph further next week. News received unofficially that Eden visit to Rome
                    complete failure. Impossible to estimate when hostilities may begin but Italian
                    Legation urging remaining Italians to hasten departure. British Minister has
                    plans for Legation evacuation but I intend to remain unless <pb facs="0980"
                        n="878" xml:id="pg878"/> instructed to go. My despatch 17<anchor n="83"
                        xml:id="d750-f1"/> recommended including two Jackson negroes in destitute
                    group.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">George</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
